,422,11,5052,317,12670,468,11,434,280,36,284,320,19,13,20,14523,17,11,16,14523,17,1215,434,284,320,20,11,220,18,317,7633,4346,313,36,313,35,1215,4038,4346,313,37,313,35,317,1502,20912,36,73315,468,11,451,1215,2383,20912,37,73315,434,11,41074,317,16119,4346,1215,16119,5349,1215,16119,3025,1215,16119,5432,1215,16119,10722,1215,16119,7832,317,1502,20912,87,73315,320,16,11,220,16,13,20,701,328,1215,2383,20912,87,73315,320,17,11,220,16,701,328,97883,1215,2383,20912,87,73315,320,17,11,481,16,701,451,71722,71722,97883,317,1502,20912,88,73315,320,20,13,20,48920,18,11,659,20,14523,18,701,328,1215,2383,20912,88,73315,320,21,13,20,48920,18,11,220,15,5905,2383,20912,88,73315,320,20,48920,20,11,481,16,13,20,48920,18,1106,1502,20912,16,16,15,61,35702,43298,31716,44970,17,13,20,11,18,13,20,5905,2383,20912,16,15,15,61,35702,43298,31716,44970,21,13,20,14523,17,11,18,13,20,1106,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn quadrilateral $ABCD$, angle $BAD$ and angle $CDA$ are trisected as shown. What is the degree measure of angle $AFD$?\n\n[asy]\nsize(150);\npair A , B, C, D; A = (0,0); B = (2, 4); C = (7,4); D = (7, -2);\ndraw( (0,0)--(2,4) -- (7,4) -- (7, -2)-- cycle);\nlabel(\"$A$\", A, SW);\nlabel(\"$B$\", B, NW);\nlabel(\"$C$\", C, NE);\nlabel(\"$D$\", D, SE);\npair E, F;\nE = (4.5-.2,1-.2); F = (5, 3);\ndraw(A--E--D); draw(A--F--D);\nlabel(\"$E$\", E, N); label(\"$F$\", F, NW);\ndot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(D);dot(E);dot(F);\nlabel(\"$x$\", (1, 1.5), S); label(\"$x$\", (2, 1), S+W); label(\"$x$\", (2, -1), N+N+N+W);\nlabel(\"$y$\", (5.5+.3, .5-.3), S); label(\"$y$\", (6.5+.3, 0)); label(\"$y$\", (5+.5, -1.5+.3));\nlabel(\"$110^{\\circ}$\",(2.5,3.5)); label(\"$100^{\\circ}$\",(6.5-.2,3.5));\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f00cfcb8cfd2c96605522b067b790f8f5ac29f62a2f95bc1c559688fa1720255"},"seconds":40.10735845565796,"seed":88131132939709701,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \\( AFD \\) in quadrilateral \\( ABCD \\), given that angles \\( BAD \\) and \\( CDA \\) are trisected.\n\nFirst, let's note the given angles:\n- \\( \\angle BAD = 3x \\)\n- \\( \\angle CDA = 3y \\)\n- \\( \\angle ABE = 110^\\circ \\)\n- \\( \\angle CDF = 100^\\circ \\)\n\nSince \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CDA \\) are trisected, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle BAD = 3x \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\angle CDA = 3y\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\( \\angle ABE = 110^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle CDF = 100^\\circ \\), we can use these to find \\( x \\) and \\( y \\).\n\n### Step 1: Calculate \\( x \\) and \\( y \\)\n\nSince \\( \\angle BAD = 3x \\) and \\( \\angle CDA = 3y \\), we know:\n\\[\n\\angle BAD = 110^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\angle CDA = 100^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n3x = 110^\\circ \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x = \\frac{110^\\circ}{3} = 36.67^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n3y = 100^\\circ \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = \\frac{100^\\circ}{3} = 33.33^\\circ\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine \\( \\angle AFD \\)\n\nTo find \\( \\angle AFD \\), we need to consider the angles around point \\( F \\). The key is to use the fact that the sum of angles around a point is \\( 360^\\circ \\).\n\nThe angles around point \\( F \\) include:\n- \\( \\angle AFD \\)\n- \\( \\angle AFE \\)\n- \\( \\angle DFE \\)\n\nSince \\( \\angle AFE = x \\) and \\( \\angle DFE = y \\), we have:\n\\[\n\\angle AFE = 36.67^\\circ \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\angle DFE = 33.33^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\angle AFD = 180^\\circ - (\\angle AFE + \\angle DFE) = 180^\\circ - (36.67^\\circ + 33.33^\\circ) = 180^\\circ - 70^\\circ = 110^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\( \\angle AFD \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{110^\\circ}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{110^\\circ}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
